From 2b8bebaa1946fa765ddc2b58e0eba5da81900c14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omalawn <omalawn@local>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:22:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] omalawn update: app updates over the link, like Flux

launcher.update_offer {name, sha256, size, offset} + one blob of at most
8 MiB receives this app's APK in order into files/omalawn-update/ (a gap or
an overlap is refused with bad_offset and
error.expected; another sha256
discards a partial file; sizes over 256 MiB are too_large). With the last
byte in, the file must match sha256 (bad_hash), be this app's own package
(not_ours), carry only signing certificates the installed app has
(wrong_key) and a versionCode no lower than the installed one (older); then
a notification "Homa Lawn update from <computer>" opens UpdateInstallActivity:
Android's installer through a dedicated FileProvider (ACTION_VIEW,
application/vnd.android.package-archive), or first the "Install unknown
apps" page for this app. Declares REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES.
launcher.app_info reports package, versionCode, versionName and the sha256
of the installed base APK. Link error objects may carry
extra fields next to code and message. The offered
file and its notification go when the app is replaced (and with the debug
hook debug_update_reset).
The update notification has its own group key, so Android (and Samsung
One UI) does not fold it together with the link's notification, where a
tap opens the launcher instead; one tap opens the installer (or the
"Install unknown apps" page). Every tap starts afresh (a left-behind
settings page is not brought back). Its text asks to allow installing
apps only while that is not allowed, and is refreshed (quietly) when the
tap finds it allowed.
